 "symmetry_statement": "U and every scheme's V_eff depend on phi only through phi^2 (and through phi in the 4x4 Hessian only via the off-diagonal entries 2 g_X^2 phi q1 and 2 h_D^2 phi D, whose sign flip is an orthogonal similarity that leaves the eigenvalues unchanged).  For a Z2-invariant initial density matrix (e.g. any thermal state above Tc, rho ~ exp(-H/T)) every Z2-odd expectation vanishes, so the probability that a correlation volume selects +v equals that of -v: p(+) = p(-) = 1/2 exactly, independent of the order of the transition.  This is a symmetry statement about the ensemble, not a dynamical result; it fails only if the state entering the transition is not Z2 invariant (preparation data outside the action).",
 "seconds": 10.042811632156372
